{"id":"mahabharata-3-166","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":166,"title":"षट्षष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 166 · The battle begins","summary":{"en":"Arjuna sees the dreadful ocean and the demons' city and blows his conch. The terrified Nivatakavachas, armed with every weapon, pour out to fight him while the sages in the sky praise him.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಭೀಕರ ಸಮುದ್ರವನ್ನೂ ದಾನವನಗರವನ್ನೂ ಕಂಡು ಶಂಖ ಊದುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಭಯಗೊಂಡ ನಿವಾತಕವಚರು ಎಲ್ಲ ಆಯುಧಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೋರಾಡಲು ಹೊರನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಆಕಾಶದ ಋಷಿಗಳು ಅವನನ್ನು ಸ್ತುತಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन भयानक समुद्र और दानवों की नगरी देखकर शंख बजाते हैं। भयभीत निवातकवच हर प्रकार के शस्त्र लेकर उनसे लड़ने निकल पड़ते हैं, जबकि आकाश में ऋषि उनकी स्तुति करते हैं।","te":"అర్జునుడు భయంకర సముద్రాన్ని, దానవ నగరాన్ని చూసి శంఖం ఊదుతాడు. భయపడిన నివాతకవచులు అన్ని ఆయుధాలతో అతనితో పోరాడడానికి బయటకు దూకుతారు, ఆకాశంలో ఋషులు అతనిని స్తుతిస్తారు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனன் கொடிய கடலையும் அசுர நகரையும் கண்டு சங்கு ஊதுகிறான். அஞ்சிய நிவாதகவசர்கள் எல்லா ஆயுதங்களுடனும் போரிட வெளியே பாய, வானில் முனிவர்கள் அவனைத் துதிக்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"ഭയങ്കരമായ സമുദ്രവും രാക്ഷസനഗരവും കണ്ട് അർജുനൻ ശംഖൂതുന്നു. എല്ലാ ആയുധങ്ങളും ധരിച്ച ഭയചകിതരായ നിവാതകവചന്മാർ അദ്ദേഹത്തോട് യുദ്ധം ചെയ്യാൻ പുറത്തുവരുന്നു; ആകാശത്തിലെ ഋഷിമാർ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ പ്രശംസിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.166; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"यक्षयुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Yakshayuddha Parva (Battle with the Yakshas)","verses":[{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततोऽहं स्तूयमानस्तु तत्र तत्र महर्षिभिः ।\nअपश्यमुदधिं भीममपांपतिमथाव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, praised here and there by great sages, I saw the dreadful ocean, the imperishable lord of waters."}},{"n":2,"text":"फेनवत्यः प्रकीर्णाश्च संहताश्च समुच्छ्रिताः ।\nऊर्मयश्चात्र दृश्यन्ते चलन्त इव पर्वताः ।\nनावः सहस्रशस्तत्र रत्नपूर्णाः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its foaming waves were scattered, heaped together and towering, and they looked like moving mountains. Thousands of ships laden with jewels lay all around."}},{"n":3,"text":"तिमिंगिलाः कच्छपाश्च तथा तिमितिमिंगिलाः ।\nमकराश्चात्र दृश्यन्ते जले मग्ना इवाद्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Timingilas, tortoises, timitimingilas and makaras were seen there, like mountains sunk in the water."}},{"n":4,"text":"शङ्खानां च सहस्राणि मग्नान्यप्सु समन्ततः ।\nदृश्यन्ते स्म यथा रात्रौ तारास्तन्वभ्रसंवृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of conches lay submerged all around, looking like stars at night veiled by thin cloud."}},{"n":5,"text":"तथा सहस्रशस्तत्र रत्नसंघाः प्लवन्त्युत ।\nवायुश्च घूर्णते भीमस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of heaps of jewels floated there, and a fearful wind whirled about; it was a marvel."}},{"n":6,"text":"तमतीत्य महावेगं सर्वाम्भोनिधिमुत्तमम् ।\nअपश्यं दानवाकीर्णं तद्दैत्यपुरमन्तिकात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Crossing that swift and excellent store of all waters, I saw nearby the city of the daityas, thronged with danavas."}},{"n":7,"text":"तत्रैव मातलिस्तूर्णं निपत्य पृथिवीतले ।\nनादयन्रथघोषेण तत्पुरं समुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Matali quickly dropped to the ground and, making the chariot rumble, rushed toward the city."}},{"n":8,"text":"रथघोषं तु तं श्रुत्वा स्तनयित्नोरिवाम्बरे ।\nमन्वाना देवराजं मां संविग्ना दानवाभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the chariot's roar like thunder in the sky, the danavas took me for the king of the gods and were alarmed."}},{"n":9,"text":"सर्वे संभ्रान्तमनसः शरचापधराः स्थिताः ।\nतथा शूलासिपरशुगदामुसलपाणयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With minds bewildered they all stood holding arrows and bows, and others held spears, swords, axes, maces and clubs."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततो द्वाराणि पिदधुर्दानवास्त्रस्तचेतसः ।\nसंविधाय पुरे रक्षां न स्म कश्चन दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Terrified, the danavas shut the gates. After arranging the city's defense, not one of them could be seen."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततः शङ्खमुपादाय देवदत्तं महास्वनम् ।\nपुरमासुरमाश्लिष्य प्राधमं तं शनैरहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I took up the loud conch Devadatta and, standing close to the asura city, slowly blew it."}},{"n":12,"text":"स तु शब्दो दिवं स्तब्ध्वा प्रतिशब्दमजीजनत् ।\nवित्रेसुश्च निलिल्युश्च भूतानि सुमहान्त्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"That sound filled the sky and rang back as an echo; living beings, even the great ones, trembled and hid."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततो निवातकवचाः सर्व एव समन्ततः ।\nदंशिता विविधैस्त्राणैर्विविधायुधपाणयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the Nivatakavachas, from every side, armored in many kinds of mail and with various weapons in hand,"}},{"n":14,"text":"आयसैश्च महाशूलैर्गदाभिर्मुसलैरपि ।\nपट्टिशैः करवालैश्च रथचक्रैश्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"with iron spears, maces, clubs, pattishas, swords and chariot wheels, O Bharata,"}},{"n":15,"text":"शतघ्नीभिर्भुशुण्डीभिः खड्गैश्चित्रैः स्वलंकृतैः ।\nप्रगृहीतैर्दितेः पुत्राः प्रादुरासन्सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"with shataghnis, bhushundis and bright, finely ornamented blades, the sons of Diti appeared by the thousand."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो विचार्य बहुधा रथमार्गेषु तान्हयान् ।\nप्राचोदयत्समे देशे मातलिर्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, studying the ground in many ways, Matali drove the horses onto level terrain, O best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":17,"text":"तेन तेषां प्रणुन्नानामाशुत्वाच्छीघ्रगामिनाम् ।\nनान्वपश्यं तदा किंचित्तन्मेऽद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Driven by him the horses went so fast that I could no longer see anything of the enemy, and it seemed a wonder to me."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततस्ते दानवास्तत्र योधव्रातान्यनेकशः ।\nविकृतस्वररूपाणि भृशं सर्वाण्यचोदयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the danavas there urged on, many times over, their whole bands of warriors, all of them with strange voices and forms."}},{"n":19,"text":"तेन शब्देन महता समुद्रे पर्वतोपमाः ।\nआप्लवन्त गतैः सत्त्वैर्मत्स्याः शतसहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that great din, mountain-like fish by the hundred thousand leapt up in the sea as living creatures fled."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततो वेगेन महता दानवा मामुपाद्रवन् ।\nविमुञ्चन्तः शितान्बाणाञ्शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the danavas rushed at me with great speed, loosing sharp arrows by the hundred and the thousand."}},{"n":21,"text":"स संप्रहारस्तुमुलस्तेषां मम च भारत ।\nअवर्तत महाघोरो निवातकवचान्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A tumultuous and dreadful clash began between them and me, O Bharata, which was to be the destruction of the Nivatakavachas."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततो देवर्षयश्चैव दानवर्षिगणाश्च ये ।\nब्रह्मर्षयश्च सिद्धाश्च समाजग्मुर्महामृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then divine sages, sages of the danavas, brahmin sages and siddhas came together at that great battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"ते वै मामनुरूपाभिर्मधुराभिर्जयैषिणः ।\nअस्तुवन्मुनयो वाग्भिर्यथेन्द्रं तारकामये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wishing me victory, those sages praised me with fitting, sweet words, as one praises Indra in the battle with Taraka."}}]}]}